description:
Found 2026-07-30 while running the first live triage e2e (gonk-dxo, issue 16 on project 75).

The onboarding MR seeds a project's .gonk.yml ladder from the operator's instance ladder at onboarding time. That ladder is then a static allow-list in the project repo. When the operator later renames or replaces rungs, every previously-onboarded project's ladder stops intersecting the operator rung list, the effective ladder goes empty, and pkg/gonkcfg/resolve.go:163 fails closed:

  'ladder empty: no rung allowed by all layers (...)'

The project flips to StateDisabled and every webhook is silently dropped with gonk_intake_dispatch_dropped_total{reason="state_disabled"}. Concrete instance: project 75 was seeded with [qwen-local, glm-test]; the operator config now defines [qwen3-14b, qwen3-6-35b, claude-sonnet]. The project has been silently off ever since.

Failing closed is CORRECT and should not change. The problem is that it is SILENT: nothing tells the project owner their ladder went stale. The DisabledReason is computed and carried on the wire (meterapi.ProjectResolution.DisabledReason) but nothing surfaces it to a human - no comment on the repo, no alert, no log line at WARN from intake.

Options worth weighing:
 (a) intake logs the DisabledReason at WARN on state transition into disabled (cheapest, no forge write);
 (b) a PrometheusRule alerting on gonk_intake_projects{state="disabled"} > 0;
 (c) the reconciler opens/updates an issue or MR on the project explaining the stale rung and proposing the new ladder (most useful, most invasive);
 (d) rung ALIASES in operator config so renames stay backward-compatible.
